@startuml 05-capture-sequence
' Copyright 2026 Muhammad Salah
' SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
title PortCloak — Capture Snapshot Sequence (offline export, one realm)

actor User
participant "Wails UI" as UI
participant Orchestrator as O
participant "Executor\n(local/ssh/docker/k8s)" as X
participant "AdminApiClient\n(verification)" as API
participant "ManifestBuilder" as MB
participant "Packager" as P
participant "CryptoVault" as CV
participant "BlobStore\n(storage backend)" as S
participant "Resilience" as R

User -> UI : Select environment + realm, Start
UI -> O : StartCapture(job)
O -> X : Probe() - reachability, kc.sh path,\nKC version, free space, free ports
X --> O : TargetFacts

alt docker / kubernetes
  O -> X : Materialise ephemeral clone\n(same image, hung, labels stripped)
  note right of X : serving instance is never\nexec'd into - see diagram 15
  X --> O : clone Running
end

O -> X : exec kc.sh export (offline)\ninto /tmp/portcloak-<id>, free ports
X --> O : exit code + streamed stdout/stderr

O -> X : Stream artifacts back (tar)
X --> R : each chunk (retry/resume on drop)
X --> O : realm-export.json, users-*.json, keys

alt verification enabled (running server reachable)
  O -> API : verify secrets are real, not masked
  API --> O : secret presence report
  O -> API : detect custom themes / provider JARs
  API --> O : external dependency list (reported, not migrated)
end

O -> X : Destroy ephemeral clone + temp dir\n(runs on success AND failure)

O -> MB : Build manifest from artifacts + verification
MB --> O : RealmManifest + CompletenessReport

O -> P : Package (tar + zstd) + IntegrityTree(sha256)
alt encryption opted in
  P -> CV : Encrypt bundle (age / AES-256-GCM)
  CV --> P : sealed bundle
end
P --> O : snapshot.pck

O -> S : Put(snapshot.pck) [multipart / resumable]
S --> R : upload with backoff + checkpoint
S --> O : stored location + remote checksum
O -> UI : progress events + final summary
UI -> User : Success + completeness report

@enduml
